  "semantics": {
    "mode": "Own RM PDF54-55: MODE=0 crystal requires OSC32_IN/OUT analog; MODE=1 bypass requires OSC32_IN digital input and permits OSC32_OUT GPIO. Both <=1 MHz; this cohort retains nominal 32768 Hz.",
    "enable_lock": "CR1 PDF70: KEY=0x5A5A in bits31:16; LSEEN bit4, LSELOCK bit5, LSECCS bit6. LSELOCK only blocks software clearing LSEEN. It is not a pad or parameter lock; do not claim the lock itself is a POR-only irreversible latch.",
    "configurable_ccs": "Own CR1 PDF70 defines CLKCCS bit8, HSECCS bit7 and LSECCS bit6 as configurable 0/1 controls. Unlike x030/F020 mandatory-write-one evidence, unrelated CLKCCS/HSECCS must be preserved by this bounded LSE operation.",
    "monitor_policy": "On a new admitted source start, enable only its LSECCS while preserving CLKCCS/HSECCS and unrelated CR1 controls. Exact enabled reuse must already have LSECCS and stable unchanged LSI; reject incompatible inherited monitor policy without repairing it. This is the proposed software health contract.",
    "failure": "Own PDF60-61: startup windows 1/1/1/2 seconds count 256/1024/4096/16384 LSE edges. Running detector needs software-enabled LSI: 128 LSE edges per 256 LSI cycles. STABLE is not a frequency measurement; SYSCLK fallback to HSI establishes no RTC fallback or elapsed-time continuity.",
    "gpio": "Own RM PDF147-156: DIR+0, ANALOG+0x1C; no SPEED, LOCK, HIGHIE, LOWIE. No LSE PINLOCK field. Never manufacture those registers from another family.",
    "gate_reset": "Own SYSCTRL PDF79-84: gates active-high, reset active-low. APBEN1/APBEN2 offsets are 0x38/0x34; APBRST1/APBRST2 are 0x48/0x44. Gate inspection needs open/readback/restore without reset or retained-user writes.",
    "consumers": "RTC full pristine snapshot regardless of SOURCE; standalone AWT SRC3 irrespective EN; all UART SOURCE2; MCO SOURCE6; only exact bonded direct routes PB12 AF3/PF1 AF1. L031F8U6 has neither direct output pad. No reset, flag clear or retained-consumer reconfiguration during admission."
  },
