    "nominal_hz": 32800,
    "documented_operating_range_percent": [
      -10,
      10
    ],
    "facts": "The own manual leaves the full LSI reset value unspecified, requires parameters before enable, forbids parameter changes after enable, and specifies reading the factory flash calibration value into LSI.TRIM. Own SystemInit performs that load; own RCC_LSI_Enable repeats it and sets WAITCYCLE=3 before enable.",
    "bounded_admission_recommendation": "Preserve inherited enabled LSI without any trim/wait write. For disabled LSI whose TRIM already equals the masked factory halfword, preserve all parameters and permit software enable after rejecting LSIRDY enable/pending state; retained consumers are not reconfigured. Only when TRIM differs, require repeated unchanged disabled/nonstable state and no selected retained user, then write only factory TRIM while preserving WAIT and every other bit; read back before enable. Then enable and poll STABLE with a bounded attempt count. This is a conservative software admission policy inferred from documented enable/calibration/consumer controls, not a separate hardware STOP guarantee.",
    "stop_observability": {
      "dedicated_stopped_bit": false,
      "LSIEN_zero": "Documented disabled control state; never sufficient by itself for ownership release.",
      "STABLE_zero": "Not stable; it does not independently prove physical stopping.",
      "software_guard": "Before changing mismatched TRIM, require CR1.LSIEN=0, LSI.STABLE=0 and ISR.LSISTABLE=0 in repeated unchanged snapshots, with all documented retained selectors and detector users absent. Do not clear sticky LSIRDY or use it as the live status."
    },
