    },
    "cold_start_sequence": [
      "Finish ordinary LSE preflight, exact package checks, pristine RTC and gate/reset inspection before LSI or oscillator/pad mutation.",
      "For enabled LSI, preserve all parameters; reject unstable state or incompatible inherited monitor conditions. Never stop or retune it.",
      "For disabled LSI with factory-matching TRIM, do not write TRIM/WAIT or inspect/reconfigure otherwise retained users; reject existing LSIRDY enable/pending, then enable and verify unchanged parameters. Starting previously disabled LSI can resume selected consumers and does not establish earlier elapsed-time continuity.",
      "For disabled LSI with mismatched TRIM, inspect the complete listed retained-user set through checked temporary configuration gates; reject asserted reset or readback failure and restore gates. Reject reserved source encodings and existing IER.LSIRDY/ISR.LSIRDY without clearing them. Hold maskable-IRQ exclusion. Capture CR0/CR1/LSI/live ISR state twice, require unchanged disabled/nonstable source and absent users. GPIOA also needs AHBEN/AHBRST bit4.",
      "Read the immutable factory halfword at 0x00100A02; its low ten bits are TRIM. Recheck the disabled state immediately before mutation. Preserve matching trim and WAIT; otherwise update only TRIM and verify exact low-ten-bit readback while still disabled.",
      "Enable only LSIEN using CR1 KEY while preserving CCS, other enables and lock state. Bounded-poll LSI.STABLE and verify preserved trim/wait plus LSIEN. Do not use attempt counts as milliseconds.",
      "After stable monitored prerequisites exist, configure/start LSE under its separate no-retained-user guard and enable only LSECCS, preserving CLKCCS/HSECCS. Freeze/readback the LSI parameters for later source-health checks.",
      "Failure is bounded and does not stop/reset/reconfigure any inherited source or clear flags. Revalidation and any concurrency exclusion must be enforced by the implementation."
    ],
    "health_policy": "The monitored held source requires LSECCS=1, LSIEN=1, LSI.STABLE=1, and unchanged LSI TRIM/WAIT; STABLE alone is not a measured LSI frequency."
